  "item": [
    {
      "id": "30566dce-e678-429b-bab4-c9715d6541cf",
      "name": "Connectors",
      "description": {
        "content": "Connectors are integrations that trigger a Bem workflow from an external system.\n\nA connector binds an inbound source — currently Box or a Paragon-managed integration such as\nGoogle Drive — to a specific workflow (by `workflowName` or `workflowID`). When the source\nobserves a new file, Bem invokes the bound workflow against that file.\n\nUse these endpoints to create, list, and remove connectors. The fields used at create time\ndepend on the connector `type`: Box connectors require Box credentials and a folder to watch,\nwhile Paragon connectors carry a `paragonIntegration` identifier and an integration-specific\n`paragonConfiguration` object (for example, `{ \"folderId\": \"...\" }` for Google Drive).",
        "type": "text/plain"
      },
      "item": [
